# ROLE
You are a senior frontend architect and design-systems engineer working with a design director. Build a complete, production-quality, responsive React landing page for "Xelofia", an AI automation platform, matching the six attached reference screenshots as faithfully as possible.

PRIORITY ORDER: (1) visual fidelity to the reference, (2) responsive correctness, (3) accessibility, (4) code quality, (5) performance. Never trade fidelity for a generic SaaS pattern.

# HOW TO WORK (follow in order)
1. ANALYSE the six screenshots. Image 1 is an overview board; images 2-6 are section details. Black or grass-photo areas around screenshots are viewer backgrounds, NOT part of the site. Recreate only the white website canvas.
2. PLAN briefly: file tree, component list, asset manifest, token list. Keep the plan under 40 lines.
3. BUILD every section and every file in full. No "rest of code here", no omitted sections, no stub components other than the explicitly-allowed route stubs in section 9.
4. VALIDATE against the checklist in section 14 and report results honestly. Do not claim you ran builds, tests or browsers you cannot run; instead say what must be verified manually.
5. OUTPUT every file with its full path as a heading, followed by the complete contents.

# 1. STACK (fixed)
- React 18+ with Vite, JavaScript (JSX). No Next.js, Vue, Angular, Bootstrap.
- Tailwind CSS v3.4 (tailwind.config.js + postcss.config.js + autoprefixer). Map all design tokens into the Tailwind theme AND CSS custom properties.
- react-router-dom for routing (needed for footer/nav destinations; see section 9).
- framer-motion (or "motion") ONLY where it genuinely helps (accordion height, tab indicator, carousel). Prefer CSS for everything else.
- lucide-react for icons (thin 1.5px stroke, 18-20px). No other icon libraries.
- clsx + tailwind-merge via a `cn()` helper in src/lib/utils.js.
- Aceternity UI: it is a copy-paste component collection, NOT an installable package. Implement locally, in the Aceternity style (Tailwind + framer-motion, in src/components/ui/), only these: (a) animated tab indicator for the FAQ tabs, (b) a subtle hover-lift card wrapper, (c) an optional text-reveal wrapper for section headings. Do not import from any "aceternity" package. Do not add more.
- Avoid every other dependency.
- Deployment target: Vercel, static output in `dist`.

